            <ArticleTitle>Spinal cord stimulator activation by an antitheft device. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>961-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a case in which electrical injury to the central nervous system resulted from uncontrolled activation of a cervical spinal cord stimulation device by an antitheft device. The injury resulted in long-term neurological sequelae.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
